{#
   The panel's own document.

   Not a variant of `layout.html.twig` and not a flag on it: the site's layout
   carries a search bar, a currency switcher, a cookie notice, a footer of 231
   city links, and fourteen external assets -- jQuery, Bootstrap, Font Awesome,
   sweetalert, a range slider, a datepicker. Measured on the sign-in page
   before this existed: 48KB of HTML and eighteen link/script tags, for one
   password field. None of it is for the person running the site (A3.5, #230).

   **Bootstrap came back in A10.1 (#287)**, on purpose and scoped to the panel:
   growing panel functionality changed the tradeoff A3.5 made, and a licensed
   dashboard template (Orchid) gives tables, forms, cards and charts already
   built. What did not come back is the CDN -- Bootstrap, its icon font and
   Inter are vendored into `public/` from the official npm packages, the same
   way the typeface already was, so the panel still fetches nothing from off
   this server. The palette, the type and the shell are Orchid's own, as
   bought -- see `admin.css`'s own docblock for why that is not the site's
   teal any more.

   `Routes::EXCLUDE_HEADER_FOOTER` looks like the lever for this and is not: it
   means "emits its own payload", for JSON. This is a different document, not
   the absence of one -- and `Kernel::wrapped()` lets it through untouched
   because it opens with a doctype.
#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-admin>
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">

    {# Nobody should ever arrive here from a search engine. #}
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">

    <title>{% block title %}Admin{% endblock %} &middot; {{ config('app.name') }}</title>

    {# The stored theme before the first paint, for the reason the site's own
       header gives: a stylesheet cannot read localStorage and a script at the
       foot runs after the paint, so a dark reader would see the light palette
       flash on every navigation. The same key as the public side, so choosing
       dark out there means dark in here. `data-bs-theme` is set alongside
       `data-theme` so Bootstrap's own component colours never disagree with
       ours -- the same pairing `global.js`'s toggle already keeps in step on
       the public site.

       The collapsed sidebar reads the same way and for the same reason: a
       class Bootstrap's `defer`red bundle applied after paint would still
       show the full-width rail for one frame. `data-rail-collapsed` sits on
       `<html>` rather than `<body>`, because `<body>` does not exist yet
       while this still runs in `<head>`. #}
    <script>
        (function () {
            try {
                var choice = window.localStorage.getItem('tb-theme');

                if (choice === 'light' || choice === 'dark') {
                    document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', choice);
                    document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-bs-theme', choice);
                }

                if (window.localStorage.getItem('tb-admin-rail-collapsed') === '1') {
                    document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-rail-collapsed', '');
                }
            } catch (e) {}
        }());
    </script>

    <link href="{{ asset(config('site.directory.css') ~ '/bootstrap.min.css') }}" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="{{ asset(config('site.directory.css') ~ '/admin.css') }}" rel="stylesheet">
</head>
<body class="shell{% block shell_class %}{% endblock %}">

{% block shell %}
    {# One rail, one well, the rail fixed and permanent beside it -- Orchid's
       own layout, not a flag on the public one. #}
    {% include 'admin/partials/rail.html.twig' %}

    <div class="well">
        <header class="well__top">
            <div class="well__lead">
                {# One button, two jobs: `railToggle()` in `admin.js` opens the
                   mobile drawer below `lg` and collapses the rail to icons at
                   `lg` and up, the same button Orchid's `data-orchid-sidebar-toggle`
                   is. #}
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-icon well__toggle" data-rail-toggle aria-controls="adminRail" aria-label="Toggle navigation">
                    <i class="bi bi-list" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </button>
                <h1 class="well__title">{% block heading %}{{ block('title') }}{% endblock %}</h1>
            </div>

            <div class="well__tools">
                {% block tools %}{% endblock %}

                <button type="button" class="btn btn-icon js-theme well__theme" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Toggle dark theme">
                    <i class="bi bi-sun-fill well__theme-icon well__theme-icon--sun" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <i class="bi bi-moon-stars-fill well__theme-icon well__theme-icon--moon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </button>
            </div>
        </header>

        {# `tabindex="-1"` so the skip link can put focus here, the same reason
           the public layout gives for its own landing point. #}
        <main class="well__body" id="main" tabindex="-1">
            {% block content %}{% endblock %}
        </main>
    </div>
{% endblock %}

<script src="{{ asset(config('site.directory.js') ~ '/bootstrap.bundle.min.js') }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ asset(config('site.directory.js') ~ '/admin.js') }}" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
